  <notes>Right margin: "Meteran. libr. 22. p. mihi 444." (the 444 is set on its own line below the note) and "Xenoph. libr. Ex. ped. Cyri, p. mihi 100." No reference marks in the text. "Sylvamducis" and "hostead" are doubtful readings of run-together or unclear letters. Long s throughout is printed as a form resembling f and is transcribed as s. "Generosissimum" and "sistere" are read from long-s forms. The running head is in the top centre, the page number at the top right.</notes>
